{
  "kanda": "bala",
  "sarga": 21,
  "title": "Vishvamitra's anger; Vasishtha appeases Dasharatha",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga21/balasans21.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/baala/sarga21/balaitrans21.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "The ire of sage Vishvamitra is shown at king Dasharatha. To pacify sage Vishvamitra, sage Vashishta intervenes and convinces king Dasharatha to send Rama with sage Vishvamitra. While doing so, sage Vashishta enumerates the capabilities of sage Vishvamitra, his knowledge of weaponry. Vashishta also suggests that all those weapons will be given to Rama, if Rama is dispatched with Vishvamitra. At last, Dasharatha agrees to send Rama."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकिरामायणे आदिकाव्ये बालकाण्डे एकविंशः सर्गः ||",
    "Thus, this is the 21st chapter in Bala Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1.21.1",
      "label": "1.21.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं तस्य स्नेहपर्याकुलाक्षरम् |\nसमन्युः कौशिको वाक्यं प्रत्युवाच महीपतिम्",
      "iast": "tat śrutvā vacanam tasya sneha paryākulākṣaram |\nsamanyuḥ kauśiko vākyam prati uvāca mahīpatim",
      "translation": "On hearing the wavery words of Dasharatha that are full of fond for his son, Vishvamitra wrathfully replied this sentence to the king.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tasya sneha paryaakula aksharam",
          "iast": "tasya sneha paryākula akśaram",
          "devanagari": "तस्य स्नेह पर्याकुल अक्शरं",
          "meaning": "his [Dasharatha's,] with fond [for son,] wavery, letters [words]",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tat vachanam shrutwaa",
          "iast": "tat vacanam śrutvā",
          "devanagari": "तत् वचनं श्रुत्वा",
          "meaning": "that, sentence, on hearing",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa manyuH kaushikaH",
          "iast": "sa manyuḥ kauśikaḥ",
          "devanagari": "स मन्युः कौशिकः",
          "meaning": "with, wrath, Vishvamitra",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahii patim vaakyam prati uvaacha",
          "iast": "mahī patim vākyam prati uvāca",
          "devanagari": "मही पतिं वाक्यं प्रति उवाच",
          "meaning": "to land, lord - king",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.2",
      "label": "1.21.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "पूर्वमर्थं प्रतिश्रुत्य प्रतिज्ञां हातुमिच्छसि |\nराघवाणामयुक्तोऽयं कुलस्यास्य विपर्ययः",
      "iast": "pūrvam artham prati śrutya pratijñām hātum icchasi |\nrāghavāṇām ayuk{}to'yam kulasya asya viparyayaḥ",
      "translation": "\"On promising me to fulfil my object in the first instance you wish to repudiate it now, undeserving is this kind of deviation for the kings of Raghava dynasty.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "puurvam artham pratishrutya",
          "iast": "pūrvam artham pratiśrutya",
          "devanagari": "पूर्वं अर्थं प्रतिश्रुत्य",
          "meaning": "firstly, object - promise, having promised",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pratij~naam haatum icChasi",
          "iast": "pratijñām hātum icchasi",
          "devanagari": "प्रतिज्ञां हातुं इच्छसि",
          "meaning": "promise, to repudiate, you wish [now]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ayam viparyayaH",
          "iast": "ayam viparyayaḥ",
          "devanagari": "अयं विपर्ययः",
          "meaning": "this, deviation",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raaghavaaNaam asya kulasya a yuktaH",
          "iast": "rāghavāṇām asya kulasya a yuktaḥ",
          "devanagari": "राघवाणां अस्य कुलस्य अ युक्तः",
          "meaning": "for [kings of] Raghava-s, this, dynasty's, not, deserving.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.3",
      "label": "1.21.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "यदीदं ते क्षमं राजन् गमिष्यामि यथागतम् |\nमिथ्याप्रतिज्ञः काकुत्स्थ सुखी भव सबान्धवः",
      "iast": "yad idam te kṣamam rājan gamiṣyāmi yathā āgatam |\nmithyā pratijñaḥ kākutstha sukhī bhava su hṛd vṛtaḥ",
      "translation": "\"If this is worth while to you, oh, king, I wish to go away as I have come, and you with your feigned promises be nonchalantly happy with your kinsmen.\" So said Vishvamitra to the king.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raajan",
          "iast": "rājan",
          "devanagari": "राजन्",
          "meaning": "oh, king",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "idam te kshamam yadi",
          "iast": "idam te kśamam yadi",
          "devanagari": "इदं ते क्शमं यदि",
          "meaning": "this is, to you, worth while, if",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "yathaa aagatam gama iSyaami",
          "iast": "yathā āgatam gama iṣyāmi",
          "devanagari": "यथा आगतं गम इष्यामि",
          "meaning": "as, I have come, to go away, I wish",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kaakutha",
          "iast": "kākutha",
          "devanagari": "काकुथ",
          "meaning": "oh, Kakutstha",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mithyaa pratij~naH",
          "iast": "mithyā pratijñaḥ",
          "devanagari": "मिथ्या प्रतिज्ञः",
          "meaning": "one with feigned, promise",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sa baandhava sukhi bhava",
          "iast": "sa bāndhava sukhi bhava",
          "devanagari": "स बान्धव सुखि भव",
          "meaning": "with, kinsmen, happy, you be [nonchalant.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.4",
      "label": "1.21.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "तस्य रोषपरीतस्य विश्वामित्रस्य धीमतः |\nचचाल वसुधा कृत्स्ना विवेश च भयं सुरान्",
      "iast": "tasya roṣa parītasya viśvāmitrasya dhīmataḥ |\ncacāla vasudhā kṛtsnā devānām ca bhayam",
      "translation": "When that prudent sage Vishvamitra is thus enwrapped in fury, then the whole earth trembled and the gods are scared.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "dhiimataH",
          "iast": "dhīmataḥ",
