          "iast": "tasya viśvamitrasya roṣa parītasya",
          "devanagari": "तस्य विश्वमित्रस्य रोष परीतस्य",
          "meaning": "that, Vishvamitra, in fury, when he is enwrapped in",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kR^itsnaa vasudhaa chachaalaH",
          "iast": "kṛtsnā vasudhā cacālaḥ",
          "devanagari": "कृत्स्ना वसुधा चचालः",
          "meaning": "entire, earth, trembled",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "suraan bhayam vivesha cha",
          "iast": "surān bhayam viveśa ca",
          "devanagari": "सुरान् भयं विवेश च",
          "meaning": "to gods, scare, entered [in their minds.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.5",
      "label": "1.21.5",
      "numbers": [
        5
      ],
      "devanagari": "त्रस्तरूपं तु विज्ञाय जगत्सर्वं महानृषिः |\nनृपतिं सुव्रतो धीरो वसिष्ठो वाक्यमब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "trasta rūpam tu vijñāya jagatsarvam mahān ṛṣiḥ |\nnṛpatim suvrato dhīro vasiṣṭho vākyam abravīt",
      "translation": "On knowing the appalled appearance of the entire world at the fury of Vishvamitra, Vashishta the great sage with high vows and an insightful one too, said these words to the king.",
      "notes": [],
