          "iast": "śrīmān",
          "devanagari": "श्रीमान्",
          "meaning": "glorious one",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dharmam haatum na arhasi",
          "iast": "dharmam hātum na arhasi",
          "devanagari": "धर्मं हातुं न अर्हसि",
          "meaning": "ethics, to forsake, not, apt of you.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.7",
      "label": "1.21.7",
      "numbers": [
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "त्रिषु लोकेषु विख्यातो धर्मात्मा इति राघव |\nस्वधर्मं प्रतिपद्यस्व नाधर्मं वोढुमर्हसि",
      "iast": "triṣu lokeṣu vikhyāto dharmātmā iti rāghava |\nsva dharmam pratipadyasva na adharmam voḍhum arhasi",
      "translation": "\"In three worlds you are renowned as the right-minded one, oh, Raghava, hence adhere to your own uprightness, and adhering to unrighteousness will be unapt of you.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raaghava",
          "iast": "rāghava",
          "devanagari": "राघव",
          "meaning": "oh, Raghu's descendent",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dharmaatmaa iti",
          "iast": "dharmātmā iti",
          "devanagari": "धर्मात्मा इति",
          "meaning": "right-minded one, thus as",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "triSu lokeshu vikhyataH",
          "iast": "triṣu lokeśu vikhyataḥ",
          "devanagari": "त्रिषु लोकेशु विख्यतः",
          "meaning": "in three, worlds, you are renowned",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sva dharmam pratipadyasva",
          "iast": "sva dharmam pratipadyasva",
          "devanagari": "स्व धर्मं प्रतिपद्यस्व",
          "meaning": "your own, uprightness, adhere to",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "a dharmam voDhum na arhasi",
          "iast": "a dharmam voḍhum na arhasi",
          "devanagari": "अ धर्मं वोढुं न अर्हसि",
          "meaning": "un-righteousness, to bear [adhering to,] not, apt of you.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.8",
      "label": "1.21.8",
      "numbers": [
        8
      ],
      "devanagari": "प्रतिश्रुत्य करिष्येति उक्तं वाक्यमकुर्वतः |\nइष्टापूर्तवधो भूयात्तस्माद्रामं विसर्जय",
      "iast": "prati śrutya kariṣye iti uk{}tam vākyam akurvataḥ |\niṣṭāpūrta vadho bhūyāt tasmāt rāmam visarjaya",
      "translation": "\"Promising to effectuate something in any way and not effectuating the given word results in the perdition to the merits of iSTapurta Vedic rituals, hence oh, Raghava, leave hold of Rama.",
      "notes": [
        "In some Vedic rituals activates for social service are undertaken, and they are known as <em>iṣṭāpūrta</em> rituals, in which digging wells, lakes and other social facilities will be undertaken."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raaghavaH",
          "iast": "rāghavaḥ",
          "devanagari": "राघवः",
          "meaning": "oh, Raghava",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "iti kariSye",
          "iast": "iti kariṣye",
          "devanagari": "इति करिष्ये",
          "meaning": "this deed/way, will be done - effectuated",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pratishrutya",
          "iast": "pratiśrutya",
          "devanagari": "प्रतिश्रुत्य",
          "meaning": "having promised",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "uktam vaakyam a kurvataH",
          "iast": "uktam vākyam a kurvataḥ",
          "devanagari": "उक्तं वाक्यं अ कुर्वतः",
          "meaning": "said [promised,] word, not, doing",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "iSTapuurta vadham bhuuyaat",
          "iast": "iṣṭapūrta vadham bhūyāt",
          "devanagari": "इष्टपूर्त वधं भूयात्",
          "meaning": "[to the merits of] Vedic rituals, doom, it becomes",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tasmaat ramam vi sarjaya",
          "iast": "tasmāt ramam vi sarjaya",
          "devanagari": "तस्मात् रमं वि सर्जय",
          "meaning": "therefore, Rama, be left of - let go.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1.21.9",
      "label": "1.21.9",
      "numbers": [
        9
      ],
      "devanagari": "कृतास्त्रमकृतास्त्रं वा नैनं शक्ष्यन्ति राक्षसाः |\nगुप्तं कुशिकपुत्रेण ज्वलनेनामृतं यथा",
      "iast": "kṛtāstram akṛtāstram vā na evam śakṣyanti rākṣasāḥ |\nguptam kuiśika putreṇa jvalanena amṛtam yathā",
      "translation": "\"Whether Rama is trained in weaponry or not, demons cannot trounce Rama as long as Kushi's son Vishvamitra protects him, like the heavenly firewall that protects divine nectar.",
      "notes": [
        "In heaven an unapproachable firewall encircles the vessel of ambrosia protecting it from thieving by the demons."
