      "numbers": [
        22
      ],
      "devanagari": "इति मुनिवचनात् प्रसन्नचित्तो\nरघुवृषभश्च मुमोद पार्थिवाग्र्यः |\nगमनमभिरुरोच राघवस्य\nप्रथितयशाः कुशिकात्मजाय बुद्ध्या",
      "iast": "iti muni vacanāt prasanna citto\nraghu vṛṣabhaḥ ca mumoda pārthiva agryaḥ |\ngamanam abhiruroca rāghavasya\nprathita yaśāḥ kuśika ātmajāya budhyā",
      "translation": "Thus the prominent king from Raghu dynasty, namely Dasharatha, became serene-minded by sage Vashishta's words, and he who is supreme among other kings and who has pronounced renown, that Dasharatha then gladly and wholeheartedly consented to the travel of Rama along with the sage Vishvamitra.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raghu vR^ishabhaH",
          "iast": "raghu vṛśabhaḥ",
          "devanagari": "रघु वृशभः",
          "meaning": "in Raghu's dynasty, prominent one, - Dasharatha",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "iti muni vachanaat",
